A static reflection for the car paint.

Every car shader in `baseq3r/scripts/cars.shader` starts with a `map $dynamicreflection`
stage: a reflection renderergl2 renders live into a cube map. This port builds
renderergl1, which has no such image, rejects the stage, and so drops the whole shader -
the cars drew as bare wheels and frames. In renderergl1 the name now resolves to
`textures/reflect/chrometest2`, the static environment map 28 of the game's own chrome
shaders use (falling back to white if it is ever missing), so the paint reads as
reflective without the cube map.

--- a/engine/code/renderergl1/tr_shader.c
+++ b/engine/code/renderergl1/tr_shader.c
@@ -624,6 +624,18 @@
 				stage->bundle[0].image[0] = tr.whiteImage;
 				continue;
 			}
+			// The car paint's reflection. renderergl2 renders it live into a cube map; this
+			// renderer has none, and rejecting the stage dropped the whole shader - the cars
+			// drew as bare wheels and frames. A static environment map the game's own
+			// chrome shaders use stands in, so the paint still reads as reflective.
+			else if ( !Q_stricmp( token, "$dynamicreflection" ) )
+			{
+				stage->bundle[0].image[0] = R_FindImageFile( "textures/reflect/chrometest2",
+					IMGTYPE_COLORALPHA, IMGFLAG_MIPMAP );
+				if ( !stage->bundle[0].image[0] )
+					stage->bundle[0].image[0] = tr.whiteImage;
+				continue;
+			}
 			else if ( !Q_stricmp( token, "$lightmap" ) )
 			{
 				stage->bundle[0].isLightmap = qtrue;
